  "note": "Extracted by hand from the o-ring stem seal edition, the JD grammar with the seal side swapped. The stem seal and seat position reads OR, ORP and ORT, the PEEK and Teflon seats keeping their Cv 3.5 and above bracket, and the stem seal detail runs the six o-ring materials. The model list adds the 978EMV motor valve and drops the inline N forms. The motor valve takes the CML rows alone, the CML100 holding its printed 0.2 to 5.0 Cv span, and its reverse CML250 row prints DIR, the sheet's own slip, held for John. The pre-combined blocks and their slashed zeros are carried as on the JD edition.",
